# The same client with one function for every request (#160). `latest` still asks without data: a `GET`, left. `call`
# is handed data that may be `None`, so whether it asks or sends is decided at run time, and the `Request` that
# `remove` opens is built with a method that is a value: the code does not say which way either goes, and the feed is
# in neither domain nor codomain.

route feeds.latest
line entry > latest call
line Web(feeds.example.org) > latest own        # return urlopen(FEED).read()

side entry left
side Web(feeds.example.org) left

route feeds.call
line entry > call call
line call > Web(feeds.example.org) own          # urlopen(FEED, data), `data: bytes | None`

side entry left
side Web(feeds.example.org) between

route feeds.remove
line entry > remove call
line remove > Web(feeds.example.org) own        # urlopen(Request(.., method=method))

side entry left
side Web(feeds.example.org) between
